<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Android 12+ (API 31+) backup and transfer rules: EXCLUDE EVERYTHING, in every mode.
  User decision 2026-10-09 (item 6): backup is off in 1.0.11. Pointed to by
  android:dataExtractionRules in AndroidManifest.xml; pinned by
  app/src/test/.../hygiene/BackupDisabledManifestTest.kt.

  Why every section is written out: "If there are no rules for a particular backup mode, such as
  if the <device-transfer> section is missing, that mode is fully enabled for all content except
  for no-backup and cache directories" (developer.android.com/identity/data/autobackup, "XML
  config syntax"). And allowBackup="false" alone is documented NOT to stop device-to-device
  transfer on some manufacturers' devices for an app targeting 31+
  (developer.android.com/guide/topics/manifest/application-element, android:allowBackup).

  tools:ignore="FullBackupContent" on the root: the lint bundled with AGP 8.2.2 checks this file against the OLD
  list of five domains and reports device_root, device_file, device_database, device_sharedpref as errors
  (measured 2026-10-09: 12 [FullBackupContent] errors across both rule files), but the documentation lists all
  nine for the data-extraction-rules format (developer.android.com/identity/data/autobackup, "XML config
  syntax", Android 12 or higher). The documentation is followed; the lint lags.

  path="." with every domain = the whole app storage: app files (getFilesDir, which holds the
  Firebase installation ID file), databases, shared preferences, external app files, and the
  device-protected counterparts. There is no <include> anywhere; <exclude> takes precedence
  over <include> in any case.

  NOT written: <cross-platform-transfer> (transfer to non-Android devices). The page
  (developer.android.com/identity/data/autobackup, "Configure Cross-Platform Transfers") says it is
  available from Android 16 QPR2 (API 36.1), that the platform attribute's only value is "ios",
  and that the section must carry <platform-specific-params bundleId teamId contentVersion> which
  match the app to its counterpart on the other platform. NeuralChek has no iOS counterpart, so
  there is nothing to put in those attributes, and an incomplete section is worse than none. The
  page does not say what a MISSING <cross-platform-transfer> section means (it says it of a missing
  <device-transfer> only), so this mode is NOT shown to be closed by this file. Not measured, not
  documented: left for the coordinator.

  The older android:fullBackupContent file (backup_rules.xml) is IGNORED on Android 12+ once
  this file is pointed to (developer.android.com/about/versions/12/behavior-changes-12,
  "Backup and restore"), and is the mechanism for Android 11 and lower.
-->
<data-extraction-rules xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools" tools:ignore="FullBackupContent">
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
        <exclude domain="external" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_sharedpref" path="." />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
        <exclude domain="external" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_sharedpref" path="." />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
